  "description": "spec/matching.md section 20 (SF20): the grammar of a session's etny-si input rows and close rows, which both trustedzones, the validators' members and the runners' session clients hold to; a row outside it is answered by the enclave with the malformed notice and kept out of the input root on every side. Accepted and refused rows read for order 7, and a row list read for it in the request's order.",
  "generator": "spec/make/session-rows.js",
  "specification": "spec/matching.md section 20",
  "order": 7,
  "grammar": [
    "input-row = \"v1\" \":\" seq \":\" orderId \":\" cid \":\" sha256    ; exactly five fields",
    "close-row = \"v1\" \":\" \"close\" \":\" orderId [ \":\" depth ]",
    "seq, orderId = plain decimal (\"0\" | nonzero *digit), at most 2^64 - 1",
    "depth = 1*9 digit",
    "cid, sha256 = any bytes but \":\"; not part of the acceptance"
  ],
  "rule": "the row's value is read as its bytes stand: nothing trimmed, folded or decoded. An input row is taken for an order when it is in the grammar, names the order and its seq is the next expected one (from 0); a gap or a duplicate is skipped on every side. The root of the taken rows is over their whole values (field 7 of the result, as result-v5.json's session example computes it). A close row names the order's close and, with a depth, its landing depth, at most the network's session_landed_depth_max_blocks (etny-nodenithy v3/networks.yaml).",
  "whys": [
    "version",
    "fields",
    "seq",
    "orderId",
    "depth",
    "otherOrder"
  ],
